# Known findings for scripts/check-template-directives.sh, deferred rather than
# suppressed. Each record names the issue that will close it.
#
# Format, tab-separated, five fields:
#
#   <rule>  <template>  <subject>  <issue>  <reason>
#
#   rule      unguarded-evidence | state-file-read
#   template  repository-relative path
#   subject   state name for unguarded-evidence, gate name for state-file-read
#   issue     owner/repo#N -- required; a record without one is an error
#   reason    why it is deferred rather than fixed
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. The check reads this file, so a
# record landing here is a deliberate, dated decision rather than a silence.
#
# Why these four are deferred: putting a when clause on work-on.md's research
# state changes when a /work-on run stops for the agent, a behaviour change to
# a shipped skill that is separate work from landing the lint (a lint that
# cannot land until the defects it finds are fixed does not land). The three
# execute.md escalate states no longer assemble a failure_reason; the edge
# into each writes it. What remains is an accepts block nothing reads.
# Removing it is a template change of its own, and terminal-retention_test.sh
# pins escalate's.

unguarded-evidence	skills/work-on/koto-templates/work-on.md	research	tsukumogami/shirabe#333	The research state is silently skipped: koto advances through it on entry, so the directive asking for codebase research never reaches the agent and its context_summary is never submitted. Fixing it changes a shipped skill's behaviour and belongs in its own change.
unguarded-evidence	skills/execute/koto-templates/execute.md	escalate	tsukumogami/koto#202	Declares failure_reason, but the attention tick chains through it before the agent could supply one. It no longer assigns from that evidence: spawn_and_await's edge writes the reason from the gate's counts. The accepts block is vestigial until it is removed.
unguarded-evidence	skills/execute/koto-templates/execute.md	escalate_dirty_merge_state	tsukumogami/koto#202	Same shape: declares a rationale the chained tick never supplies. It no longer assigns failure_reason, so ci_monitor's reason, with the rationale submitted there, is what the run ends with.
unguarded-evidence	skills/execute/koto-templates/execute.md	escalate_upstream_drift	tsukumogami/koto#202	Same shape: declares a rationale the chained tick never supplies. It no longer assigns failure_reason, so worktree_discipline_check's reason, with the rationale submitted there, is what the run ends with.
